invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: rsa_sign64_key_ok returns without wiping the words of q, so the
  prime stays in the dead frame after every signature and every init. The
  answer is the same, so no test of the key test's verdict notices.
  bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test copies the stack below the key test and finds
  two words of q there.

--- old
    ct_wipe(p, sizeof p);
    ct_wipe(q, sizeof q);
--- new
    ct_wipe(p, sizeof p);
